# Nightly AI-app upkeep: brew-upgrade the AI coding apps but codex and
# claude-code (the weekly upgrade owns those), re-capture the
# skills/MCP/agent/plugin inventory, then commit and push it; emails only when
# something changed.
#
# The commit is part of this job because the inventory is this job's own
# output. Leaving it dirty made `git status` permanently noisy in a checkout
# three sessions share, which is how a real edit hides, and the churn rode
# onto whatever branch somebody switched to next.
#
# It runs at 04:30, well after repo-sync-nightly (02:45). Jobs that commit
# and push to the same repository each pull --ff-only before they push, so
# the ordering is what keeps their fast-forwards from racing rather than the
# retry nobody wrote.
JOB_SCHEDULE="30 4 * * *"
JOB_COMMAND="sh \"$ROOT/../local-ai-apps/ai-apps.sh\" nightly"
